## Redesign the domain navbar context rail

Context: Task 4 required aligning the canonical navbar contract and public
documentation with the shipped L1/L2 context-rail implementation, then running
the full automated verification workflow without claiming manual browser checks.

Changes:

1. .cursor/11-frontend-design.mdc
   Updated the canonical L1/L2 navbar contract to document the L2 domain context
   launcher, remove obsolete `#domainL1Link` references, and align action order
   with the current Versions → Close → Save rendering (`bi-123`).
2. docs/architecture.md
   Added the architecture-level navbar context rail contract (identity launcher,
   workspace-map behavior, active/inactive workspace semantics, and mobile icon
   state).
3. docs/user-guide.md
   Updated end-user navigation guidance for the L2 identity target, workspace
   map launch behavior, active workspace static segment behavior, and responsive
   icon-only rail state, including the Versions (`bi-123`) action wording.
4. src/front/static/global/css/components.css
   Corrected the workspace-map documentation comment to reference
   `#domainContextTrigger`.
5. src/front/templates/partials/layout/_workspace_map_modal.html
   Corrected the workspace-map template comment to reference
   `#domainContextTrigger`.
6. src/front/static/global/css/main.css
   Finalized context-rail styling: removed stale L1-only dead CSS, preserved
   segmented workspace styling and active ordinal behavior, and documented
   constrained/mobile behavior (breadcrumb collapse, icon-only actions/targets
   below breakpoints, no horizontal overflow, dropdown escape preserved).
7. tests/units/front/test_settings_subnav_hidden.py
   Replaced the stale L1 Domain expectation with a contract asserting
   `updateDomainMenuVisibility` no longer references legacy L1 selectors
   (`domainNav`, `domainL1NavItem`, `domainL1Link`).
8. src/front/templates/base.html
   Confirmed the L2 context trigger + segmented rail structure and preserved
   action ordering with the Versions action before Close and Save.
9. src/front/static/global/js/navbar.js
   Updated workspace-map binding and L2 visibility comments to match the
   shipped L2 domain identity/context trigger contract.
10. tests/units/front/test_segmented_subnav_contract.py
    Kept the segmented subnav contract aligned with L2 context trigger
    structure, workspace ordering, and constrained/mobile behavior gates.
11. tests/units/front/test_workspace_map_modal.py
    Kept workspace-map trigger/open/highlight contracts aligned with
    `#domainContextTrigger` and modal launch behavior.
12. tests/units/api/test_ui_rendering.py
    Renamed the navbar contract test to reflect the L2 context trigger
    contract while preserving assertions.
13. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-18-navbar-context-focus-rail-design.md
    Corrected feature wording to the shipped Versions label and `bi-123` icon.
14. docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-18-navbar-context-focus-rail.md
    Corrected plan wording to the shipped Versions label and right-side action
    order.
15. Follow-up refinement (L2 context badge)
    Locked the L2 context trigger to `200px`, matched its fixed rail height
    with `.ob-subnav-workspace-list`, moved the context copy to a two-row grid
    (status row + ellipsized name row) with a right-side raw numeric version
    column spanning both rows, scoped the local status badge `ms-2` removal in
    `.ob-subnav-context-copy`, aligned the whole trigger to selected-state
    styling (`--db-primary-light` surface with primary-darker text/border),
    emphasized that version cell with
    `--db-primary-darker` + `--db-on-primary` and larger bold numerals, added a
    small explicit row gap between status and name without increasing shared
    rail height, set the shared context/workspace control height to `3.5rem`,
    tightened shell vertical rhythm to 4px above/below the L2 rail
    (`.ob-subnav-nav` top padding `0.25rem`; desktop `.sidebar-layout` padding
    `0.25rem 0.5rem 0.5rem`), and fixed mobile icon-only context behavior by
    resetting the icon to normal flow and using explicit icon-control trigger
    sizing.
16. Settings-page return-to-domain behavior
    Added a mutually exclusive Settings presentation in the single `#obSubnav`
    slot: with a loaded domain, show only `#settingsDomainReturnLink` ("Back to
    domain") and hide the regular domain rail (`#domainWorkspaceSubnavNav`),
    breadcrumb, and actions; with no loaded domain, keep L2 hidden. The return
    link reuses `openWorkspaceMap()` and falls back to `/domain/` without JS.
17. Geometry follow-up hardening and contract cleanup
    Consolidated `.ob-subnav-context-trigger` selected-state styling to a
    single declaration source while preserving the shared
    `.ob-subnav-context-trigger, .ob-subnav-workspace-list` height/box geometry
    source; removed redundant mobile physical padding declarations in favor of
    `padding-inline`; updated contracts to assert non-redundant logical mobile
    padding and shared-rule intent; aligned L2 action-order comments to
    Versions → Close → Save; and synchronized mobile spec wording to icon-only
    selected-color context behavior with hidden status/name/version details.
18. Settings return-link width parity refinement
    Locked `#settingsDomainReturnLink` / `.ob-settings-domain-return-link` to an
    exact desktop/tablet `200px` outer width (`width/min-width/max-width`) to
    match the expanded sidebar and shared left gutter alignment, centered its
    icon+label composition within that width, and added a mobile width reset
    (`width: auto`, `min-width: 0`, `max-width: none`) to prevent viewport
    overflow.
19. Settings first-paint and compact rail refinement
    Prevented `breadcrumb.js` from revealing the shared breadcrumb on Settings
    before asynchronous navbar state resolves, and reduced the shared domain
    context/workspace rail height from `3.5rem` to `3rem` while preserving the
    4px gaps above and below the L2 controls.
20. Near-full-height workspace target surfaces
    Stretched direct `.ob-subnav-workspace-list > .ob-subnav-item` and their
    `.ob-subnav-link` targets with `height: 100%` so hover and selected
    backgrounds fill the available inner rail height (~40px) while preserving
    the outer `3rem` rail and `0.2rem` inset. Added a static contract test and
    synchronized the canonical frontend design rule. Browser verification
    measured all four desktop/mobile targets at `39.625px` inside the `48px`
    rail with equal insets, healthy dropdown/focus behavior, and no overflow.

